{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552608-v5-a-sourcebook-for-my-chronicle","id":1552608,"title":"(V5) A Sourcebook for my Chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-23T07:26:13-07:00","id":1552608,"title":"(V5) A Sourcebook for my Chronicle","content":"Hello, Kindred. <br /> A while ago (actually, about a year ago), I made a post here asking you all for ideas and suggestions on Gehenna scenarios \u2014 ways I could present it to my players.<br /> <br /> Well, that chronicle happened. And it lasted for quite a while. And it was... quite an experience. My players and I got deeply involved in the story, in the characters, and in the plot, to the point that once the main arc concluded, we started organizing one-shots within the same universe \u2014 exploring the past of secondary characters, simultaneous narratives told from different perspectives, and so on. The universe we affectionately called the \u201cGehenna&quot; began to grow and become its own thing. I think you all understand exactly where this is going.<br /> <br /> The main chronicle ran for about six months, with the spin-offs adding another month and a half. Unfortunately, one of the players started to seriously get on my nerves with her behavior at the table, which deeply demotivated me from continuing as a storyteller \u2014 especially since this universe had become very important to me. So I let it go.<br /> <br /> Now, thanks to my wife, I remembered why I own every single V5 sourcebook and why I got so attached to this universe in the first place. I remembered why I love VtM so much. And I think Gehenna is worthy of its own sourcebook. One that I can share with all of you \u2014 maybe giving you the chance to experience something close to what we felt.<br /> <br /> I already have the first frameworks complete, and I\u2019m currently working on:<br /> <br /> - the general context of New York in 2021, in a post-pandemic time that sparked tension among the Kindred;<br /> <br /> - a mechanical system of puzzles made by Kindred for Kindred, called the Shadow Game;<br /> <br /> - new characters, usable both as SPCs and PCs;<br /> <br /> - the return of some forgotten clans and bloodlines, adapted to V5\u2019s \u201cgrounded versatility\u201d system;<br /> <br /> - and of course, most importantly, the Gehenna scenario the universe proposes.<br /> <br /> I will finish this sourcebook.<br /> Or I won\u2019t let myself suffer the Final Death.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28353-nicknickeo","name":"NickNickeo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28353_4.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-04T17:58:34-07:00","id":1553629,"title":"","content":"I'm rooting for you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-07T09:38:58-07:00","id":1553683,"title":"","content":"Good luck with this project!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","cu